    "body": "Quick gate result for PR #1952, head ae2620c15cb0aaf34ef56d7bd6dc620655c91ff4.\n\nCommands, run in a new worktree of this head:\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --dry-run`\n- `cargo test -p xtask -j 6`\n\nWhy not the full quick gate: the dry run selects 33 steps. Most of them build the camcraft-post and camcraft-app suites. The change touches xtask, and a new worktree needs a full build of those crates. This did not fit the 30 minute budget. The run used `cargo test -p xtask -j 6` instead.\n\nResult of `cargo test -p xtask -j 6`:\n- unit tests (xtask, src/main.rs): pass, 141 passed, 0 failed\n- tests/merge_ready_skill.rs: pass, 3 passed, 0 failed\n- tests/review_artifacts.rs: pass, 3 passed, 0 failed\n\nDry run: 33 steps in the quick plan, and the plan has one step for each test binary (for example one step per post suite and per app suite, plus the xtask unit tests). The dry run was ok for all 33 steps. The plan steps themselves did not run.\n\nThe timing comparison against the old gate was not measured.\n",
